From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lemelson <97357844+Lemelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:07:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] decoder: force the first picture of a paused seek

A seek while the input is paused restarts buffering with
vlc_input_decoder_StartWait() (b_first = b_waiting = true). Because the
decoder is paused, vlc_input_decoder_Wait() returns without waiting for
data, and es_out calls vlc_input_decoder_StopWait(), which clears
b_waiting. An asynchronous decoder (avcodec frame threads, VideoToolbox)
returns the target picture only after that.

ModuleThread_PlayVideo() forces the first picture only when
b_first && b_waiting. The target picture then reaches the video output
with b_first=1, b_waiting=0 and b_force=0. It is scheduled against the
frozen, paused clock and dropped as late. Time and position report the
new target, but the screen keeps the pre-seek frame until playback
resumes.

Also force the first picture while the decoder is paused. b_first is
cleared on the spot, so exactly one picture is forced, and playback
does not advance.

Reproduction (libvlccore at 4ca4eb0c3e, macOS arm64):
 - open a generated 60 s video file, play, then pause;
 - while paused, seek with vlc_player_SetTime(), vlc_player_SeekByTime()
   (absolute or relative) or vlc_player_SetPosition();
 - the displayed picture PTS stays on the pre-seek frame.
Reproduced on the unmodified core with software avcodec and with
VideoToolbox + samplebufferdisplay, before any interface code receives
a frame (LLDB at the drop: b_first=1, b_waiting=0, b_force=0). The
stock macOS (VLCPlayerController) and Qt (PlayerController) interfaces
call the same player API with no paused-specific path, so stock VLC 4
is affected. A NextVideoFrame-based workaround in the interface shows
the target, but breaks the following resume and clean shutdown.

This hunk is narrow and the first upstream candidate. Test:
redesign/patches/engine/tests/run-paused-seek-smoke.sh (12 failures on
the unpatched core in video mode; all four topologies pass with the
whole series).

Possibly related upstream reports (found by title, not verified):
https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc/-/issues/25315
https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc/-/issues/22456

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/decoder.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/input/decoder.c b/src/input/decoder.c
index 0988eb6..514bc80 100644
--- a/src/input/decoder.c
+++ b/src/input/decoder.c
@@ -1519,7 +1519,9 @@ static int ModuleThread_PlayVideo( vlc_input_decoder_t *p_owner, picture_t *p_pi
             return VLC_ENOENT;
     }
 
-    if( p_owner->b_first && p_owner->b_waiting )
+    /* Buffering may stop waiting before the first asynchronous paused picture
+     * arrives. It still needs a forced display without advancing playback. */
+    if( p_owner->b_first && (p_owner->b_waiting || p_owner->paused) )
     {
         msg_Dbg( p_dec, "Received first picture" );
         p_owner->b_first = false;
